Subject: Serve assets from a mapping of the extracted tree when one is named

CORDIAL_ASSET_MMAP_DIR names a directory holding the APK's assets already
extracted (cordial-import makes one per build, sealed read-only). A read is then
served from a MAP_PRIVATE mapping of that file instead of a decompressed copy in
a leaked, process-private buffer: the pages are the page cache's, shared between
clients and reclaimable while clean. The mapping is never unmapped, so the
pointer AAsset_getBuffer returned stays valid for the life of the process, which
is the contract Vec::leak gave. A size that differs from the APK entry, a
symlink, or a name that leaves the tree falls back to reading the APK.
Unset, nothing changes. Includes a test run against a real mapping.

--- a/crates/cordial-runtime/src/android/asset.rs
+++ b/crates/cordial-runtime/src/android/asset.rs
@@ -137,7 +137,76 @@
